      "title": "Overview",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "block_1",
          "text": "The chapter begins by calling for several forms of prayer\u2014for everyone and specifically for rulers. Its stated aim is a tranquil, quiet, dignified life marked by godliness, rather than political loyalty to those rulers.",
          "verse_refs": [
            "1 Timothy 2:1-4"
          ],
          "evidence_ids": [
            "1tim-prayer"
          ],
          "synthesis_ids": [
            "syn_historical_context_8e8a0a7b401b"
          ],
          "confidence": "high",
          "interpretation_level": "fact"
        },
        {
          "id": "block_2",
          "text": "Verses 3\u20137 hold together God\u2019s desire that all be saved, the one mediator, Christ Jesus, and his self-giving ransom for all. These affirmations are explicit, but broader conclusions about exactly how salvation works for all people remain disputed.",
          "verse_refs": [
            "1 Timothy 2:1-4",
            "1 Timothy 2:1-7",
            "1 Timothy 2:13-14",
            "1 Timothy 2:15",
            "1 Timothy 2:3-6"
          ],
